RESPONSE: According to the Wikipedia article on Hallstatt (SOURCE: Hallstatt.txt | relevance=9.0), Hallstatt is a small town in the Gmunden District of the Austrian state of Upper Austria. It is situated between the southwestern shore of Hallstätter See and the steep slopes of the Dachstein massif, in the Salzkammergut region.

